I see exactly what went wrong. I made a scoping error in the code I gave you.
I placed the borderColor: (theme) => index <= activeStep... logic inside the <Stepper connector={...}> prop. However, the connector sits *outside* the .map() loop, which means index doesn't exist there! That is what caused the React ReferenceError crash.
Let's fix this cleanly. We will use the CustomConnector at the top of your file to handle the line alignment, and remove the buggy inline code from the grid completely.
### Step 1: Fix the CustomConnector Alignment
At the top of your JournalAuthorization.jsx file (around line 112), update your CustomConnector variable so the lines strike exactly through the middle of the 22px circles:
```javascript
const CustomConnector = styled(StepConnector)(({ theme }) => ({
  [`&.${stepConnectorClasses.alternativeLabel}`]: {
    top: 11, // Exactly half of the 22px circle height
    left: 'calc(-50% + 11px)',
    right: 'calc(50% + 11px)',
  },
  [`&.${stepConnectorClasses.active}`]: {
    [`& .${stepConnectorClasses.line}`]: { borderColor: theme.palette.success.main },
  },
  [`&.${stepConnectorClasses.completed}`]: {
    [`& .${stepConnectorClasses.line}`]: { borderColor: theme.palette.success.main },
  },
  [`& .${stepConnectorClasses.line}`]: {
    borderColor: theme.palette.divider,
    borderTopWidth: 2,
    borderRadius: 1,
  },
}));

```
### Step 2: Fix the Grid Column (Remove the Crash)
Now, find the workflowState column in your columns array. Replace its renderCell with this corrected version that removes the index error and uses the clean CustomConnector:
```javascript
    {
      field: "workflowState",
      headerName: "Workflow Progress",
      width: 250,
      align: "center",
      headerAlign: "center",
      disableColumnMenu: true,
      sortable: false,
      renderCell: (params) => {
        const state = params.value || "PENDING_L1";
        const workflow = params.row.approvalWorkflow || "Workflow_3";
        const isRejected = state === "REJECTED";

        if (isRejected) {
          return <Chip label="REJECTED" color="error" size="small" variant="filled" sx={{ mt: 1.5, fontWeight: "bold" }} />;
        }

        let stepLabels = ['L1', 'L2', 'L3', 'Final'];
        if (workflow === 'Workflow_4' || workflow === 'W2_4_APPROVERS') {
          stepLabels = ['L1', 'L2', 'L3', 'L4', 'Final'];
        }

        let activeStep = 0;
        if (state.includes("L2")) activeStep = 1;
        else if (state.includes("L3")) activeStep = 2;
        else if (state.includes("L4")) activeStep = 3;

        if (state === "POSTED" || state === "SCHEDULED" || state === "APPROVED") {
          activeStep = stepLabels.length;
        }

        return (
          <Box sx={{ width: '100%', display: 'flex', alignItems: 'center', height: '100%' }}>
            <Stepper
              activeStep={activeStep}
              alternativeLabel
              connector={<CustomConnector />} // Back to the clean, error-free connector
              sx={{ width: '100%', mt: 0.5 }}
            >
              {stepLabels.map((label, index) => {
                const isCompleted = index <= activeStep;
                
                return (
                  <Step key={label} completed={isCompleted}>
                    <StepLabel
                      StepIconProps={{
                        sx: {
                          width: 22,
                          height: 22,
                          color: isCompleted ? 'success.main' : 'text.disabled',
                          '&.Mui-completed': { color: 'success.main' },
                          '&.Mui-active': { color: isCompleted ? 'success.main' : 'primary.main' }
                        }
                      }}
                      sx={{ p: 0, m: 0 }} // Removes padding that shifts the line
                    />
                  </Step>
                );
              })}
            </Stepper>
          </Box>
        );
      },
    },

